Dear SeqFans,

I have computed and certified the first 40,000 decimal digits of the
Golomb-Dickman constant

  lambda = integral_0^infinity exp(-u - E_1(u)) du
         = 0.624329988543550870992936383100837244...

The certificate consists of integers Lambda_- < Lambda_+ and a scale
S = 133074 such that lambda lies in [Lambda_-/2^S, Lambda_+/2^S] and

  floor(10^40000 Lambda_- / 2^S) = floor(10^40000 Lambda_+ / 2^S).

The interval therefore does not cross a decimal cell, and the 40,000
digits are proved by truncation rather than merely computed in floating
point. Its width is about 10^-40042.26, leaving roughly 42 guard digits.

Method: the trapezoidal rule after the Takahashi-Mori substitution, with
explicit tail and discretisation bounds (Trefethen-Weideman), Stieltjes
continued fractions for E_1, and Arb balls for every node. The trust base
is Arb plus the cited theorems; this is not a proof-assistant
formalisation.

I have prepared a b-file for A084945 with terms n = 0..39999, extending
the current n = 0..101:

  https://github.com/fix27/golomb-dickman-constant/tree/main/40000

  SHA-256 c73af643198da299d2e624e3c2f69d05439efcddbbefa7cec176ac63f993bed3

The verifier uses only the Python standard library:

  python verify_40000.py
  OK: 40000 digits certified

Two small extensions of A225242 follow from the certified string: the
blocks 55555 and 666666 do not occur among the 40,000 digits, so
a(5), a(6) > 40000 (the entry recorded a(5) > 15000).

I have submitted the b-file to the OEIS editors. If an editor can help
with the upload, or advise on the preferred size (10,000 / 20,000 /
40,000 terms), I would be grateful.

Comments, corrections and independent checks are very welcome.

